{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014LBZfwKb4kd3FaGFMmp6hG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user productivity + R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings, plain-text source of truth). Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a personal productivity dashboard.** A self-contained Python-stdlib web server (`anchor_gui.py`) runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`, reading and writing markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`) directly. Tasks move through a lifecycle â€” active â†’ done/cancelled/saved-for-later/restored â€” via an interactive browser GUI, with a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`) for the same operations.\n\n- **Markdown is the database.** No DB, no lock files, no binary formats â€” every task, project, and idea is plain text editable from the GUI, CLI, or any editor. A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity, every endpoint, and the full task-state machine, writing dated reports.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\" for trio-driven development** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). This turns each project into a cockpit that launches and tracks research/planning/build work as durable, isolated server-side sessions. It's shipped through four design generations:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated summaries, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, deliverable pin/declare, and an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the one sanctioned native dep, `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (hard-guarded off port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built + merged to master 2026-06-13, merge `38fd70e`) â€” one terminal substrate that auto-loads a lane's skill once and greets once (killing a repeating-prompt bug), an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), Paradigm-2 inline expanding lane tiles with status lights, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass idea board with promote-to-lane, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **What it ships:** the running Anchor service/dashboard itself (the pinned flagship deliverable), the CLI engine, the daily health-check harness, desktop launchers/shortcuts, and the layered R&D modules (`rnd_registry`, `effort_history`, `sessions`, `summarizer`, `pty_manager`, `session_registry`, `worktrees`, `terminal_session`, `handoff`, `preview_server`, `deliverables`, etc.) â€” plus vendored front-end assets (xterm.js, anchor-term, the GWL brand mark) and frozen design/plan docs under `planning/rnd-v2â€¦v4/`.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the git status shows uncommitted changes and new untracked artifacts (`Anchor.md`, `.anchor/projects/`, `rnd_jobs/`, `rnd_registry.json`, modified dashboards/domain files), so the working tree is currently ahead of the last commit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24709,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24709},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35a32ad8-4f69-48e6-93ab-b577e27daf29","uuid":"96021d0d-2d83-46a4-980b-1095b8669e89","request_id":"req_011Cc1Xu44TQ55mf5adW4NTF"}
